        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "26521b1a-466f-5447-a369-0d45e21e2c05",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Bands: The Innocence Mission, Starflyer 59\n- People: Karen Peris, Don Peris, Mike Bitts, Steve Brown, Jason Martin, Ronnie Martin\n- Places: Lancaster, Pennsylvania, Riverside, California\n- Works: Tending the Rose Garden, Godspell\n- Topics: folk rock, alternative rock, Catholic rock\n\nFacts:\n- The Innocence Mission is an American folk rock band centered on husband-and-wife singer-songwriters Karen Peris and Don Peris.\n- The Innocence Mission was formed in Lancaster, Pennsylvania in the early 1980s after Karen Peris, Don Peris, Mike Bitts, and Steve Brown met during a Catholic school production of \"Godspell\".\n- Tending the Rose Garden is the 1986 debut EP by the Catholic rock band The Innocence Mission.\n- Since 1995, The Innocence Mission has stylized its name on all releases as \"the innocence mission\".\n- Starflyer 59 is an alternative rock band from Riverside, California that was founded in 1993 by Jason Martin, who is the brother of Ronnie Martin of Joy Electric.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
